media: cedrus: express secondary chroma stride in hardware units

NV12 chroma stride uses half the byte pitch, as for primary output. Passing
the full pitch made 960x544 decode fault at the end of the capture mapping.
With a guard allocation it wrote 130560 bytes beyond the 783360-byte frame.

--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
@@ -717,7 +717,7 @@
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_H264_SDROT_CHROMA_ADDR, (u32)chroma);
 
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_SECONDARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE,
-		     VE_SECONDARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_CHROMA(stride) |
+		     VE_SECONDARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_CHROMA(stride / 2) |
 		     VE_SECONDARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_LUMA(stride));
 
 	reg = cedrus_read(dev, VE_CHROMA_BUF_LEN);
